\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overall framework of the proposed closed-loop perception, geometric modeling, and control system. RGB-D frames are first processed through instance segmentation (MSAM-Net) for mask refinement. The resulting point clouds undergo geometric consistency filtering (PX3C) and temporal stabilization (CAOS) to produce a reliable 3D representation. State estimation uses a Kalman-filter-based spatiotemporal approach, followed by two-stage motion planning in relative velocity space. Active interaction reduces environmental entropy and resets unstable object states, enabling robust real-time execution.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{}{figure.1}{}}
